greeting that works at any time is \"Hello.\"\n\nThe clue is in the time: **am** means before 12 noon. **pm** means after 12 noon.\n\nHere is my own contrasting pair (different times):\n\n- 10 am at work: *\"Good morning, Sara.\"*\n- 3 pm at work: *\"Good afternoon, Sara.\"*\n\nThe time changes from am to pm, so the greeting word changes too.\n\nNow look at **7:30 pm** again. Is it before or after 12 noon? Then write **one greeting** for Ahmed with a time-of-day word (not \"Hello\").","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["reteach_simpler","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_misconception_strategy_shift","level_beginner","during_feedback","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"reteach_with_simpler_step","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"question","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"a3a48ad11998da9d97771285","attemptsOnTask":1,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"repeated","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":2,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569540258-8vng","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"INCORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"SAME_ITEM","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569540258-8vng","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":2,"qualityFlags":[],"markerStatus":"ok"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-e3e87cee-6a7e-4279-9597-5462fa576e1a","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0011"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0011","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"ea0786932bbe185c"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":3,"learner":"Good morning, Ahmed! I think it is still good for evening. Morning is for all day, no? My teacher says good morning is always polite.","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569540258-8vng","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":5103,"reply":"\"Good morning\" is polite. Your teacher is right about that. But in English it is usually only for the morning, before 12 noon. In the evening it can sound strange.\n\nHere is the answer for the task:\n**\"Good evening, Ahmed!\"** 7:30 pm is in the evening.\n\nAn everyday comparison: you say \"breakfast\" in the morning and \"dinner\" in the evening. Greetings change in the same way.\n\nNew task:\nIt is **2 pm**. You meet your colleague Omar at lunch. Write **one greeting** for Omar with a time-of-day word (not \"Hello\").","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["corrective_feedback_retry","comprehensible_model"],"reasonCodes":["answer_to_question","level_novice_prompt_first","recurrence_unknown_after_shift","level_beginner","during_feedback"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"learner_retry","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"question","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"a3a48ad11998da9d97771285","attemptsOnTask":2,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"unknown","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":3,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569540258-8vng","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"INCORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"NEW_ITEM","item":"greeting-time-2","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569559723-xv08","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":0,"qualityFlags":[],"markerStatus":"ok"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-e3e87cee-6a7e-4279-9597-5462fa576e1a","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0012"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0012","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"cbe75bd82de944b7"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":4,"learner":"Good morning, Omar! It is 2 pm, but morning is still morning for me. I think good morning is fine all day.","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569559723-xv08","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":7241,"reply":"The form is still good: greeting, then the name.\n\nThe word \"morning\" is the same problem as before. Here is the answer for 2 pm:\n**\"Good afternoon, Omar!\"** In English, 2 pm is in the afternoon, after 12 noon.\n\nIn some languages, a morning greeting may be fine all day. In English, it usually is not. If you are not sure of the time, **\"Hello\"** is always safe.\n\nOne small step:\nIt is **4 pm**. You see your manager, Leila, in the office. Write **one greeting** for Leila with a time-of-day word.","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["corrective_feedback_retry","comprehensible_model"],"reasonCodes":["answer_to_instruction","level_novice_prompt_first","recurrence_unknown_after_shift","level_beginner","during_feedback"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"learner_retry","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"instruction","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"a3a48ad11998da9d97771285","attemptsOnTask":3,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"unknown","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":1,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569559723-xv08","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"INCORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"NEW_ITEM","item":"LTB-002-time-greeting","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569567931-xgez","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":0,"qualityFlags":[],"markerStatus":"ok"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-e3e87cee-6a7e-4279-9597-5462fa576e1a","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0013"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0013","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"7267d70e5f19fec9"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":5,"learner":"Good morning, Leila! It is 4 pm, but I still think morning is correct for all day. My teacher said it is polite, so I use it.","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569567931-xgez","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":5356,"reply":"The form is good again: greeting, then the name.\n\nThe correct greeting at 4 pm is:\n**\"Good afternoon, Leila!\"** 4 pm is after 12 noon, so it is the afternoon.\n\nYour teacher is right that \"Good morning\" is polite. But in English, \"polite\" and \"correct for the time\" are two different things. After 12 noon, \"Good morning\" can sound like a mistake. You can ask your teacher about this too.\n\nA simple rule: **am → morning. pm → afternoon or evening.**\n\nNew task:\nIt is **9 pm**. You arrive at your friend Karim's home for dinner. Write **one greeting** for Karim with a time-of-day word.","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["answer_with_reasoning","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_after_strategy_shift_model_then_transfer","level_beginner","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"answer_check_question","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"instruction","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"a3a48ad11998da9d97771285","attemptsOnTask":4,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"repeated","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":1,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569567931-xgez","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"INCORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"NEW_ITEM","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569574827-alzp","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":0,"qualityFlags":[],"markerStatus":"ok","revealedItemId":"msg:msg-1794569567931-xgez"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-e3e87cee-6a7e-4279-9597-5462fa576e1a","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0014"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0014","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"cefef58193b8b9c2"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":6,"learner":"Good morning, Karim! It is 9 pm, but I still think good morning is polite all day. Is it okay?","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569574827-alzp","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":7009,"reply":"People will understand you, and they will see you are being polite. But in English it is not usual. At 9 pm, \"Good morning\" sounds like a mistake about the time.\n\nThe correct greeting is:\n**\"Good evening, Karim!\"** 9 pm is in the evening.\n\nThe polite part of your greeting is \"Good ... , Karim!\" Only the time word changes:\n\n- before 12 noon → morning\n- 12 noon to about 6 pm → afternoon\n- after about 6 pm → evening\n\nLet's try a choice this time.\nIt is **8 pm**. You meet your friend Nadia at a restaurant. Which greeting is correct, **A** or **B**?\n\nA) Good morning, Nadia!\nB) Good evening, Nadia!","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["answer_with_reasoning","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_after_strategy_shift_model_then_transfer","level_beginner","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"answer_check_question","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"instruction","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"a3a48ad11998da9d97771285","attemptsOnTask":5,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"repeated","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":1,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569574827-alzp","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"INCORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"NEW_ITEM","item":"greeting-time-8pm","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569582731-ek0q","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":0,"qualityFlags":[],"markerStatus":"ok","revealedItemId":"msg:msg-1794569574827-alzp"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-e3e87cee-6a7e-4279-9597-5462fa576e1a","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0015"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0015","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"cefef58193b8b9c2"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":7,"learner":"I think A is correct. Good morning is polite, so I choose A.","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569582731-ek0q","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":6296,"reply":"The answer is **B: \"Good evening, Nadia!\"** 8 pm is in the evening.\n\nI see your reason: you want to be polite. Both A and B are polite. The difference is only the **time word**. In English, the greeting usually shows the time of day.\n\nThink of a clock:\n- 8 **am** → Good morning\n- 8 **pm** → Good evening\n\nSame polite greeting. Different time.\n\nOne tiny step:\nIt is **6:30 pm**. You see your neighbour Huda. Write only the **missing word**:\n\n\"Good ______, Huda!\"","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["answer_with_reasoning","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_after_strategy_shift_model_then_transfer","level_beginner","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"answer_check_question","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"question","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"a3a48ad11998da9d97771285","attemptsOnTask":5,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurre